[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65302,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "<p>Bartholin gland hyperplasia is a benign expansion of normal Bartholin gland tissue and ducts. Benign tumours of the Bartholin gland without and with a smooth muscle component have been termed Bartholin gland adenoma and Bartholin gland adenomyoma, respectively, but these are extremely rare.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-30T12:17:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65303,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8140/0 Adenoma NOS</p>\r\n<p>8932/0 Adenomyoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65304,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GA03.Y Other specified diseases of Bartholin gland</p>\r\n<p>GA03.Y &amp; XH3DV3 Other specified diseases of Bartholin gland &amp; Adenoma NOS</p>\r\n<p>GA03.Y &amp; XH4ZH4 Other specified diseases of Bartholin gland &amp; Adenomyoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65305,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> nodular hyperplasia of Bartholin gland</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65306,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65307,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Bartholin gland hyperplasia, adenoma, and adenomyoma arise in the region of the Bartholin glands (bilateral symmetrically located glands in the posterolateral introitus).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65308,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In the largest reported series, the average patient age was 35&nbsp;years (range: 19&ndash;56&nbsp;years) {9785128}. Presentation is usually with a painless swelling.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65309,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are uncommon lesions. Adenoma (2&nbsp;cases reported) {11109169; 9785128} and adenomyoma (1&nbsp;case reported) are extremely rare {11109169}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65310,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65311,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65312,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are usually relatively small and predominantly solid lesions, sometimes with small cystic areas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65313,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Hyperplasia consists of a nodular/lobular proliferation of morphologically bland mucinous acini with preservation of the normal acinar and ductal arrangement {9785128; 28914673; 16753743}. Inflammation and squamous metaplasia of the ducts may be present. Uncommonly, there is extensive mucin extravasation {28914673}.</p>\r\n<p>True Bartholin gland adenoma consists of a lobular arrangement of small closely packed acini and tubules lined by bland epithelium, occasionally with colloid-like secretions {11109169; 9785128}, and adjacent normal Bartholin gland elements. Bartholin gland adenomyoma has in addition a fibromuscular stromal element that is immunoreactive for desmin {9785128}. Rare cases have been associated with adenoid cystic carcinoma or epithelial&ndash;myoepithelial carcinoma {11109169; 9785128}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-30T12:17:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65314,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65315,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65316,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> hyperplasia: nodular/lobular proliferation within the Bartholin gland of morphologically bland mucinous acini, with preservation of the normal acinar and ductal arrangement; adenoma: closely packed acini and tubules contiguous with adjacent Bartholin gland elements in a circumscribed lesion; adenomyoma: an appearance similar to that of adenoma, but with a fibromuscular stromal component.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65317,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65318,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 512,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign lesions.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:28:37"
      }
    ],
